---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { LEGAL } from "../legal";
---

<Layout
  title="Code signing policy · Snap2Link"
  description="How Snap2Link's Windows installers are signed, who approves each release, and what the app sends over the network."
>
  <header class="legal-header">
    <a href="/" class="nav-brand" aria-label="Back to Snap2Link">
      <img src="/assets/logo-app-icon.png" width="28" height="28" alt="" style="border-radius: 6px;" />
      <span>Snap<b>2</b>Link</span>
    </a>
  </header>

  <main class="legal">
    <h1>Code signing policy</h1>

    <p>
      Free code signing provided by <a href="https://about.signpath.io/">SignPath.io</a>, certificate
      by <a href="https://signpath.org/">SignPath Foundation</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Status:</strong> signing is being set up. Until SignPath Foundation accepts the project,
      Windows installers are unsigned. This page will name the first signed version.
    </p>

    <h2>What is signed</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        The Windows installer, <code>Snap2Link_&lt;version&gt;_x64-setup.exe</code>, published on the
        <a href="https://github.com/amys94fr/Snap2Link/releases">GitHub releases page</a> and through
        winget.
      </li>
      <li>
        Only installers built by the GitHub Actions workflow of
        <a href="https://github.com/amys94fr/Snap2Link">amys94fr/Snap2Link</a>, from the source code at
        the release tag, on GitHub-hosted runners. Nothing built elsewhere is sent for signing.
      </li>
      <li>
        The installer's product name must be Snap2Link and its version must match the release, or the
        signing is refused.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      macOS and Linux packages are not covered by this certificate. Every update, on every platform,
      is also checked by the app against Snap2Link's own updater key before it installs.
    </p>

    <h2>Team roles</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Committers and reviewers: <a href="https://github.com/amys94fr">amys94fr</a></li>
      <li>Approvers: <a href="https://github.com/amys94fr">amys94fr</a></li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Changes from anyone else arrive as pull requests, which a committer reviews before they are merged.
      The <code>main</code> branch only accepts changes through pull requests that pass the tests. Every
      signing request is approved by hand on SignPath. All team members use multi-factor authentication
      on GitHub and SignPath.
    </p>

    <h2>Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Snap2Link only sends data to the services you choose, and to the few it needs to work:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Your captures go to the host you pick in the setup wizard: Snap2Link hosting at
        <code>i.snap2link.app</code>, or your own Google Drive.
      </li>
      <li>
        Signing in to a Snap2Link account goes through a code sent by email, or through Google if you
        choose it.
      </li>
      <li>
        Before the first upload without an account, a Cloudflare Turnstile check runs once.
      </li>
      <li>The app checks GitHub for updates.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> lists what each of them receives and how long it is
      kept. The app sends no telemetry and no analytics.
    </p>

    <h2>Report a problem</h2>
    <p>
      If you think a file signed for Snap2Link is not what it claims to be, write to
      <a href={`mailto:${LEGAL.contact}`}>{LEGAL.contact}</a>. You can also report it to SignPath at
      <a href="mailto:support@signpath.io">support@signpath.io</a>.
    </p>
  </main>

  <nav class="legal-nav" aria-label="Legal pages">
    <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a>
    <a href="/terms/">Terms</a>
    <a href="/legal/">Legal notice</a>
    <a href="/">Back to Snap2Link</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>
